<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<RSLogix5000Content SchemaRevision="1.0" SoftwareRevision="16.03" TargetType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" ContainsContext="true" Owner="Dale Reed, Rockwell Automation" ExportDate="Tue Jan 26 12:38:34 2010" ExportOptions="References Context">
<Controller Use="Context" Name="ProcessObjects">
<DataTypes Use="Context">
</DataTypes>
<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_MEQ" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="true" CreatedDate="2008-04-15T14:24:48.205Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2010-01-26T17:36:50.226Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Masked Equal (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Deleted unused Local Tag]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Performs a 64-bit bitwise comparison of a Source Value against a Compare Value,
and returns TRUE if they are the same in all bit positions which have a '1' in the Mask
Value.  In other words, the output is true if (Source AND Mask) = (Compare AND Mask).

On a False rung in LD, or in FBD with EnableIn cleared to 0, Out is cleared to 0.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="Inp_Source" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer Source Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_Mask" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer Mask for bitwise compare]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_Compare" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[64-bit signed integer  Compare Value]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1 if Source AND Mask = Compare AND Mask, 0 otherwise]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Source" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Inp_Source as a pair of DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Compare" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Inp_Compare as a pair of DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Mask" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Inp_Mask as a pair of DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If rung is false, clear output "Out"]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE LOGIC
============================================================
When EnableIn is false (false rung in LD, input of 0 in FBD),
the main Logic Routine is not scanned.
However, we still want to generate "Out" to provide animation!
============================================================
CONVERT INPUTS TO PAIRS OF 32-BIT VALUES (DINTs)
============================================================
This rung copies all the input values into pairs of 32-bit integers (DINTs) per value
so we can do the compares with 32-bit instructions.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Inp_Source,Wrk_Source[0],2)COP(Inp_Mask,Wrk_Mask[0],2)COP(Inp_Compare,Wrk_Compare[0],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
BASED ON 32-BIT COMPARES, DETERMINE OUTPUT
============================================================
If the bottom 32 bits compare OK, and the top 32 bits compare OK,
the 64-bit comparison is good and the output is SET.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Wrk_Source[0],Wrk_Mask[0],Wrk_Compare[0])MEQ(Wrk_Source[1],Wrk_Mask[1],Wrk_Compare[1])OTE(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Perform bitwise compare and output TRUE if (Source AND Mask) = (Compare AND Mask)]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_MEQ:  Masked Equal (64-bit)
============================================================
Revision 1.0-01 Release:  2010-01-26
Deleted unused Local Tag
============================================================
Performs a 64-bit bitwise comparison of a Source Value against a
Compare Value, and returns TRUE if they are the same in all bit
positions which have a '1' in the Mask Value.

In other words, the output is true if (Source AND Mask) = (Compare AND Mask).
============================================================
POWERUP / INVALID STATE HANDLING
============================================================
This logic determines a comparison result every scan when enabled
(and sets EnableOut and Out to 0 every scan if on a False Rung or if EnableIn is cleared).
No powerup or invalid state handling is necessary.
============================================================
CONVERT INPUTS TO PAIRS OF 32-BIT VALUES (DINTs)
============================================================
This rung copies all the input values into pairs of 32-bit integers (DINTs) per value
so we can do the compares with 32-bit instructions.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Inp_Source,Wrk_Source[0],2)COP(Inp_Mask,Wrk_Mask[0],2)COP(Inp_Compare,Wrk_Compare[0],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
BASED ON 32-BIT COMPARES, DETERMINE OUTPUT
============================================================
If the bottom 32 bits compare OK, and the top 32 bits compare OK,
the 64-bit comparison is good and the output is SET.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MEQ(Wrk_Source[0],Wrk_Mask[0],Wrk_Compare[0])MEQ(Wrk_Source[1],Wrk_Mask[1],Wrk_Compare[1])OTE(Out)OTE(EnableOut);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
